---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Storybook usage"
   summary="Storybook is the component path. It lets operators and agents run the same applicability, driver, pattern, and verification flows against a local story instead of a full page."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Target shape</h2>
      <pre><code>node packages/cli/dist/cli.js inspect applicable --storybook-url http://127.0.0.1:6006 --story-id forms-login--default --json
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js verify criterion 3.3.8 --storybook-url http://127.0.0.1:6006 --story-id forms-login--default --target virtual --json</code></pre>
      <p>
         The Storybook path resolves the story to an iframe URL and carries the story identity through
         the result. That keeps the evidence tied to the component fixture you actually exercised.
      </p>
      <p>
         If you are arriving from a broader task, the <a href="/workflows#agent-and-storybook">workflow page</a> is the faster map.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>What works against Storybook</h2>
      <ul>
         <li><code>inspect applicable</code> and <code>inspect criterion</code></li>
         <li><code>drive start</code> against a resolved story target</li>
         <li><code>run axe</code> and <code>run pattern</code></li>
         <li><code>verify criterion</code> and <code>verify level</code></li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Where Storybook helps</h2>
      <ul>
         <li>isolating a dialog, auth form, or live region without a full app boot</li>
         <li>feeding story metadata into applicability hints</li>
         <li>repeating the same component test path while the page-level app is still noisy or unstable</li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <h2>Local only for now</h2>
      <p>
         The first shipped Storybook path assumes a local dev server you control. It is meant to make
         component-level accessibility work faster, not to become a generic remote crawling system.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
